 to tap  into your reserves you can't be running  your business at full capacity already  you can't be running your business on  zero on empty because that means there's  no extra gear that means that when life  punches you in the face you can't handle  it that means if you want to try or  taste or test something else you can't  do it because you have no reserves you  have no battery there's no more gas in  the tank  and so that's where a lot of  entrepreneurs live that that's where  it's really Troublesome that's where a  lot of entrepreneurs will end up burning  out failing and crushing their dreams  because you're just running with no gas  left in the tank and so you can stretch  yourself I think that's normal I think  that's okay I think life will hit you in  the face and just when you think it  couldn't get worse here comes another  punch that will happen but it's making  sure that you can live that Balanced  Life whatever balance looks like for you  rule number 47 hold yourself accountable  you need people in your life to hold you  accountable because you will never push  yourself as hard as you can go you get a  personal trainer not because of what  exercises you should do you can look  that up online the real value of a  trainer is to have somebody right there  in front of you in your face telling you  to do three more reps of that exercise  when you want to quit when you're gonna  tap out and if you're by yourself you'd  say I'm done and they say give me three  more because all of the growth happens  in that last set if there's nobody  around you to hold you to a higher  standard you'll always know that there's  another level but you'll be too afraid  to reach for it yourself so let's use me  as an example  I want to solve the world's biggest  problem I don't think people believe in  themselves enough it's why I created  this Channel and all the other ones I  have and the books and the speaking  everything I do I want to go out and do  this impossible thing that's never going  to happen I'm never going to solve the  world's biggest problem and yet I wake  up every day and I try to do it and I  use a combination of what I call  aspirational mentors which are people  like Steve Jobs and Elon Musk and the  people that I profile on this channel  and then I also do it from people who  challenge me one-on-one if you watch my  entrepreneur advice Channel I get pushed  every week by my agent Steve by  psychologists in Australia by people who  are coaching me and I had to get better  and they push me and they tell me I need  to do more and they tell me I'm being an  idiot in these areas and like go this is  the homework  and the more uncomfortable I feel during  that process usually the better the  advice is if I think about the tour that  I launched last year another tour that  I'm doing this year  it started as a free tour and became a  paid tour when my agent Steve pushed me  to do it  like you need to charge for this and  immediately my heart's boom boom boom  boom boom I'm scared means I have to do  it  having people around you who can push  you to do the things that you need to do  who make you nervous who make you scared  who see your blind spots who cut through  your BS  who tell you that's just fear talking  because we'll come up with really  logical reasons why we can't do  something or aspirational mentors who  when you see how they react to things  how they see things how they understand  the world and then you look at what  you're doing it forces you to be pulled  up it forces you to take the next step  up on the staircase you need to do it  because your environment's been  perfectly designed to keep you where you  are your friends your family all of it  it's keeping you exactly where you are  and the difference between where you are  now and where you want to be and where  you can be in a year in two years in  five years in 10 years is going to be  the people you have around you and how  much they're willing to push you to  believe in you to tell you what you may  not want to hear but you need to hear to  grow to challenge yourself and get to  the next level rule number 48 own your  dreams when did you decide that your  dreams shouldn't be big when did you  decide that you shouldn't tell anyone  else about your dreams until you own  your dreams and stop making yourself  feel small those dreams will never  happen  never now this is something everybody  struggles with everybody myself Mel  everybody we're worried about playing a  bigger game we're worried about thinking  bigger for ourselves and we're worried  about telling other people because what  if it doesn't work out what if we don't  make it what's that judgment gonna come  how are they going to think about us and  so I think about my own story what I'm  trying to create the biggest fight that  I used to get into with my agent Steve  was he says Evan you need to be a  household name you need to be famous  like Steve I don't want to be famous  I I equated famous to Ego if you're  famous and you're just big eagle Maniac  I didn't I don't want to be an egomaniac  it's not it's not about me it's about  spreading belief I don't I'm nervous  getting in front of the camera even  before filming this video I'm nervous  like I wanted to wanted to do well the  lights come on I don't crave it I don't  crave attention I'm an introvert I like  just doing my thing Evan you need to get  famous why Steve why do I need to get  famous and for maybe two years we fought  over this  because I kept equating Fame with ego  and I looked at the people who were  famous and like I don't want to be like  them and there's a lot that they did  that that bothered me and I wanted to do  it a different way and that's the key  it's finding the different way to do it  how does an introvert on a mission  become famous I don't know we're gonna  go on this journey together and  hopefully find out what finally clicked  for me was him saying  when you get famous your mission will  spread  if you start tying actions to Mission  that's how you get me to move for other  people it might be hey I'll give you all  this money if you do this or you'll have  the fame or or credibility or have  statues but I don't need statues built  of me but as soon as you tie it to  Mission and service that gets me going  so he said if you actually want  to fulfill your mission if you say you  want to spread belief then you need to  get famous because the more people know  about you the more people will hear your  message and if finally it finally stuck  like okay I gotta do it I don't know how  to do it I've never I've never tried to  do it I've I've always wanted to be  behind the spotlight and so now now this  is part of my mission I need to become a  household name and get famous so that  more people can believe in themselves if  I actually want to solve the world's  biggest problem  then I need to be out there doing it I  need to believe in myself more  and if I'm trying to spread belief I  need to believe in myself more too  and so I think that's a human condition  that's part of what we want to do you  want to step outside your comfort zone  you want to serve humans are built to  serve we are we are built to serve but  service requires helping other people  and because we're afraid of judgment  you don't want to do it so you've got  your foot in the gas and a break at the  same time you want to help people but  you're worried about their judgment so  you don't do anything you know you're  capable of more you know you're capable  of more but you don't do it because  you're afraid rule number 49 kick  yourself forward bring yourself to other  people can be a fantastic thing a  fantastic thing but there's only one way  to make it work you have to kick  yourself forward not down you kick  yourself forward not down most people  here's what they do most people you see  someone who's that success you see  somebody with a Ferrari or the car or  somebody who you're jealous of or you're  insecure about yourself when you're  around them you see them and you you  think you suck you look at them and say  I suck why am I not further ahead why is  Dan who's not even 40 years old yet have  all of the success and here I am and I'm  not doing it yet  right you kick yourself down that's how  most people do it and in public you  might tell your friends how that  person's a scumbag you stole he's  ripping people off he's a jerk but when  you go home you just tell yourself man  why am I not for their head why am I why  am I here why am I stuck why am I not  getting more momentum you've been kicked  but you've been kicked down  where what you want to do is kick  yourself forward  you want to kick yourself forward if you  see Dan driving his Ferrari or you see  somebody that you look up to and respect  use it as a kick forward to say this is  what's possible this is what's possible  and if he can do it if she can do it  then I can do it too  my hero is Young Les Brown I love him  from a speaker just my favorite speaker  of all time I look at that and I say I  can get better  not that I suck it's that this is what's  possible I need to get better I need to  improve I need to practice I need to  keep going because that's what's  possible and rule number 50 the last one  before very special bonus clip is never  give up Paul Newman the legendary actor  had an amazing quote that I love to  repeat he said I check my pulse and if I  can find it I know I've got a chance  you've got a very important choice to  make you either make the rest of your  life the best of your life or you settle  for what is and live in your excuses so  you know why I would give up you know  what I'm deeply afraid of I've got two  I've got a short-term fear and a  long-term fear my short-term fear is of  disappointing people my biggest short  term in the moment fear is disappointing  people that I would show up to an event  and let people down that I wouldn't give  them value that people would come and  waste their time spend their money and I  didn't give them value I'm deeply afraid  of it and still I'm I put pressure on  these videos I want these videos to be  great every time I get in front of this  camera and start making a video I put  pressure myself that this seems to be  the best video that I've ever done I  want to not disappoint you guys every  single time and this little pause  hesitation before filming and I'll spend  a couple minutes procrastinating because  I'm I'm afraid I'm afraid of  disappointing you and making a crappy  video I'll procrastinate and then I'll  do it and I'll feel great at doing it  but my biggest short-term fear  disappointing people my biggest  long-term fear is of regret is that I  won't live my life is that I'll look  back and say I could have done more I I  should have pushed harder because you  rarely regret the things that you did  it's the things that you didn't do the  things you were too afraid to do the  action's not taken that's what you  normally regret  and so my biggest short-term fear is  disappointing people maybe because the  long-term fear is fear of regret and  those things  they fight each other  right they fight each other because if  I'm afraid of disappointing somebody I'm  not going to take the action that I  should be taking and then I'm going to  regret it later on and so I try to use  that to your potential regret to push me  into action to say if I don't make  videos today if I don't do that speech  if I don't get up and make that  presentation if I don't do the thing  that I'm afraid to do  because of disappointing people  potentially then I'll regret it  and I'll put the pressure like this is  the video this video right here this is  a video that's gonna blow up everything  that'll change the whole game for me and  if I don't record it because I'm afraid  of disappointing somebody I'm gonna  regret that my whole life and I make it  so painful for myself that then I have  to act and that pain pushes me into  action and out of procrastination mode  not have a very special bonus coat from  Evan learn how to enjoy the process but  before that it's time for the three  important Landing questions let's go  from watching the video to taking action  here we go question number one where do  you need to kick yourself forward number  two where do you need to stop hiding and  number three what is the rejection that  you need to stop fearing living a joyful  life comes from enjoying the process of  what you are doing when you wake up  every morning do you look forward to the  work that you're about to do today or do  you hate it do you dread it and want to  stay in bed if you are waking up and  going to do work that is torture to you  that you don't enjoy that you dread on a  daily basis you will never be joyful or  successful and I want to change that so  is on a call yesterday with a buddy of  mine who had built a Million Dollar Plus  business and he said Evan I don't know  what to do I'm I'm unhappy I'm depressed  I don't like my business I've built this  business that I hate going to and I'm  and I've always hated most of what I've  done I've had success I've built a  Million Dollar Plus business but I've  always hated the work and I thought you  have to hate the work to get the results  that you want  but I keep hearing you and all these  other successful people saying you gotta  love the process you gotta love the work  so what do I do man I don't know what to  do do I do I shut the whole thing down  do I keep building what do I do I'm lost  I said hey man there's something that  you love inside your business what do  you love doing and it started off was  well I like giving people strategy I  like doing the strategy part of my  business but I don't like the rest of it  okay great so Step One is you're gonna  start doing all the strategy work in  your business amazing what else like  while I also like selling okay awesome  you're gonna be the chief salesperson  you're going to be off selling and  meeting people and having conversations  it's like I don't like delivering I  don't like the operations awesome that's  why you've hired your CEO to run your  company  and then he said I also like having  conversations and mentoring people not  everybody on my team likes to be  mentored but I love mentoring people I  love guiding them so he's got three  things that he loves doing he looks  forward to that he wishes he could do  all day and luckily those are high value  skills for his business right he wants  to be able to set the strategy and help  his clients with strategy he wants to be  able to sell and he wants to be able to  mentor and guide the people on his team  he just doesn't want to deliver  so you either become a consultant where  this is all you do or you hire somebody  who he's already bought on who's your  CEO and give him more lateral give him  more abilities give him more power give  him more permission and at the same time  if he loves mentoring and training  people he loves people who will listen  to him and be open to his guidance and  wisdom then he needs to have a team who  respects him who wants that and not  everybody will you could have the  greatest person who can write copy or  the greatest programmer or the greatest  whatever for your business but if you  love mentoring and they don't want to be  mentored that's not a good fit  so you need to do an assessment on your  team and see who loves being mentored by  you and keep those people because  if you go into work every day and you  see the people who you love being with  who you love mentoring who you feel like  you're a team with you'll love going to  work but if you go to work every day and  you see these people who don't want to  listen to you who don't want to be  trained you don't want to be Mentor just  want to sit down and do their work  it's not going to be a joyful experience  for you  and that lack of Joy will mean you won't  have success in your company as well and  so he's built up this machine that he  hates because he always thought you need  to hate the work like work is work it  sucks but you get the results like no  dude it's the exact opposite you've had  success you built a Million Dollar Plus  business because you're talented but it  should have been a 10 million dollar  plus business by now and if you want  more Evan check out his top 50 rules  video the link is right there next to me  continue to believe and we'll see you  there
 

